  "package_id": "berge-triangle-spectrum",
  "formal_scope": "Lean 4.35.0 proves that paired products are Berge-triangle-free and saturated with p(n−2p) edges, that for every n ≥ 8 the explicit system J(⌊n/4⌋, n−2⌊n/4⌋) is saturated, is not a paired product and has exactly ⌊(n−1)²/8⌋ edges, and the arithmetic of the window, including the explicit deficits and at least ⌊n/4⌋ − ⌊√(2n)⌋/2 − 1 sizes there that are not of the form p(n−2p). It derives the upper spectrum and the maximum ⌊(n−1)²/8⌋ for saturated nonproducts from the containment theorem, which enters as a hypothesis and has a conventional proof, checked computationally for small orders.",
